 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The professions",
   "texto": [
    "To ask what one does: **Qu'est-ce que tu fais dans la vie ?** (literally «What are you doing in life?»).",
    "When you indicate a profession with **être**, the name usually goes without article: **Je suis médecin**, **Elle est professeur**.",
    "Many professions have feminine: **étudiant** → **étudiante**, **infirmier** → **infirmière**, **serveur** → **serveuse**, **vendeur** → **vendeuse**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "«être» plural",
   "texto": [
    "**Nous** = us. **Ils** = them. **Elles** = them.",
    "Many names and adjectives form the plural with **-s**; this mark is usually mute at the end: **étudiant** and **étudiants** sound the same.",
    "If there is at least one man in a group, **ils** is used."
   ]
  },
